// Reference book: Builtin Functions.
page builtins { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Builtin Functions"

  p "WCL ships a standard set of builtins, callable like any function. They group into collections, strings, math, tensors, and control flow."

  h2 "Collections"

  p "Higher-order and list utilities. `map` / `filter` / `fold` take function arguments."
  table {
    rows:
      | "Function"           | "Purpose" |
      | "`map(xs, f)`"       | "Apply `f` to each element" |
      | "`filter(xs, f)`"    | "Keep elements where `f` is true" |
      | "`fold(xs, init, f)`" | "Reduce to a single value" |
      | "`len(xs)`"          | "Length" |
      | "`sum(xs)`"          | "Sum of numbers" |
      | "`range(a, b)`"      | "List of integers `a`..`b`" |
      | "`head` / `tail`"    | "First element / everything after it" |
      | "`flatten` / `zip`"  | "Flatten one level / pair two lists" |
      | "`reverse` / `sort` / `unique`" | "Reorder / sort / dedupe" |
      | "`list_contains(xs, x)`" | "Membership test" |
      | "`index_of(xs, x)`"  | "Position of an element" |
      | "`at(xs, i)`"        | "Element at index" |
      | "`take(xs, n)` / `drop(xs, n)`" | "First / all-but-first `n`" |
  }

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
doubled = map([1, 2, 3], fn(x: i64) -> i64 x * 2)   // [2, 4, 6]
evens   = filter(range(0, 10), fn(x: i64) -> bool x % 2 == 0)
total   = fold([1, 2, 3], 0, fn(acc: i64, x: i64) -> i64 acc + x)
WCL
  }

  h2 "Strings"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Function" | "Purpose" |
      | "`split(s, sep)` / `join(xs, sep)`" | "Split into / join from a list" |
      | "`replace(s, from, to)`" | "Substring replace" |
      | "`contains` / `starts_with` / `ends_with`" | "Substring tests" |
      | "`to_upper` / `to_lower` / `trim`" | "Case and whitespace" |
      | "`concat(a, b)`" | "Concatenate two strings" |
      | "`format(fmt, …)`" | "Format with `{}` placeholders" |
  }

  h2 "Math"

  p "Math builtins operate in `f64`, widening integer arguments. Angles are in radians."
  table {
    rows:
      | "Group"     | "Functions" |
      | "Trig"      | "`sin` `cos` `tan` `asin` `acos` `atan` `atan2`" |
      | "Convert"   | "`radians` `degrees`" |
      | "Powers"    | "`sqrt` `cbrt` `pow` `hypot` `exp`" |
      | "Logs"      | "`ln` `log10` `log2`" |
      | "Rounding"  | "`floor` `ceil` `round` `trunc`" |
      | "Magnitude" | "`abs` `sign` `min` `max` `clamp`" |
      | "Constants" | "`pi()` `tau()` `e()`" |
  }

  h2 "Tensors"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Function" | "Purpose" |
      | "`tensor(data, shape)`" | "Build a tensor from a flat list + shape" |
      | "`tensor_data(t)` / `tensor_shape(t)`" | "Read back the elements / dimensions" |
      | "`tensor_reshape(t, shape)`" | "Reshape without copying data" |
  }

  h2 "Control flow"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Function" | "Purpose" |
      | "`error(msg)`" | "Abort evaluation with a message" |
      | "`panic(msg)`" | "Unrecoverable failure" |
      | "`assert(cond, msg)`" | "Error if `cond` is false" |
  }

  h2 "Reflection"

  p "Query the schema itself. Each takes a reference to a type / field / block / variant (a bare identifier or member path, e.g. `Image` or `Image.alt`)."

  table {
    rows:
      | "Function" | "Purpose" |
      | "`decorator_names(&T)`" | "List the decorator names attached to the target." |
      | "`decorator_arg(&T, dec, slot)`" | "Read a named argument of decorator `dec` (`none` if absent)." |
      | "`type_fields(&T)`" | "List a type's fields as records — `name`, `type`, `is_function`, `optional`, `has_default`, `is_block`, `repeated`, `accepts`, `decorators` — own fields first, then those inherited via `extends`. Drives the wdoc `type_table` component." |
      | "`ast_string(&T)`" | "Pretty-print the source behind a reference — a `type` / `interface` / `union` / `symbol_set` / `block` / field declaration — or a function value (`fn(…) -> … …`). Output is canonical (run through the formatter), so it normalises the original spacing." |
      | "`fn_signature(f)`" | "Describe a function's parameters and return type. Pass a function **value** (full structured `params` with `name`/`type`), or a built-in's **name string** (e.g. `\"map\"`) to get its parameters + help text. Returns `{ doc, params: [{name, type, doc}], return_type, signature, is_builtin }`." |
  }

  h2 "Meta"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Function" | "Purpose" |
      | "`eval(src)`" | "Parse the utf8 string `src` as a WCL expression and evaluate it in the current scope (it sees surrounding `let` bindings and document names). Returns the resulting value." |
  }
}
